Connect handler, verbatim (119-159):

```dart
Future<void> _connect(ScanResult result) async {
  await _stopScan();
  Get.dialog(
    const Center(child: CircularProgressIndicator()),
    barrierDismissible: false,
  );
  try {
    final client = CompanionClient.instance;
    await client.connect(result.device);
    if (Get.isDialogOpen ?? false) Get.back();
    if (client.state == CompanionConnState.ready) {
      await CacheData().setString(
        AppKeys.lastBleDeviceIdKey,
        result.device.remoteId.str,
      );
      CompanionNotifRelay.instance.attachIconNeed();
      await CompanionForegroundService.requestNotificationPermission();
      await CompanionForegroundService.start();
      AppTheme.snack(
        LocaleKeys.bleSnackbarTitle.tr,
        LocaleKeys.bleScanConnected.trParams({'name': _deviceName(result.device)}),
      );
      Get.back();
    } else if (client.state == CompanionConnState.versionMismatch) {
      AppTheme.snack(LocaleKeys.bleSnackbarTitle.tr, LocaleKeys.deviceMismatch.tr);
    } else {
      AppTheme.snack(LocaleKeys.bleSnackbarTitle.tr, LocaleKeys.failed.tr);
    }
  } catch (e, st) {
    if (Get.isDialogOpen ?? false) Get.back();
    AppTheme.fail(LocaleKeys.bleSnackbarTitle.tr, 'BleConnect', e, st);
  }
}
```

Progress UI while connecting/discovering = a **modal `Get.dialog(Center(CircularProgressIndicator()), barrierDismissible: false)`** — no phase text, no cancel. The AppBar has a small 20x20 spinner while `_scanning` (170-180). On success it persists the device id, attaches the notif relay, starts the Android foreground service (text "正在保持与码表的连接", `companion_foreground_service.dart:52`), toasts `bleScanConnected` ("已连接 @name"), then `Get.back()` **pops back to DevicePage**, which then fires `controller.onConnected()`. On mismatch/failure it does *not* pop — it stays on the scan page with a toast.

## 4. The auto-reconnect path (`lib/ui/shell/shell_controller.dart`)

Fields the reconnect logic reads: `conn`, `status`, `info`, `_holdLink = true` (line 54), `client => CompanionClient.instance`.

**Trigger points:**
- `onInit()` (68-82) → `unawaited(_loadStores()); unawaited(_tryReconnect());`  (ShellController is created lazily when ShellPage first builds).
- `didChangeAppLifecycleState` (92-104): `resumed` → `_tryReconnect()`; `paused`/`hidden` → `_onWentBackground()`.
- `_onWentBackground()` (114-122): if `_holdLink`, `await _tryReconnect()` then start the foreground service if a stored id exists.
- Adapter on: not here — `CompanionClient`'s own `_onAdapterState` → `kickReconnect(resetBackoff: true)` (`companion_client.dart:881-885`).
- Watchdog / disconnect backoff: inside the client (`_armWatchdog` 871-879 every 20 s; `_scheduleReconnect` 856-869 exponential 2 s→30 s), both only when `_autoReconnect && _device != null`.

Verbatim:

```dart
// shell_controller.dart:124-143
Future<void> _tryReconnect() async {
  if (!_holdLink) return;
  if (client.isReady) {
    await client.refreshTimeSyncIfDue();
    return;
  }
  if (client.isLinking) return;
  if (client.device != null && client.autoReconnect) {
    await client.kickReconnect(resetBackoff: true);
    return;
  }
  final id = await CacheData().getString(AppKeys.lastBleDeviceIdKey);
  if (id == null || id.isEmpty) return;
  try {
    await client.connect(BluetoothDevice.fromId(id));
    CompanionNotifRelay.instance.attachIconNeed();
  } catch (e) {
    await AppLog.w('Shell', '自动重连失败: $e');
  }
}
```

```dart
// shell_controller.dart:151-165
Future<void> onConnected() async {
  _holdLink = true;
  final id = client.device?.remoteId.str;
  if (id != null) {
    await CacheData().setString(AppKeys.lastBleDeviceIdKey, id);
  }
  CompanionNotifRelay.instance.attachIconNeed();
  await CompanionForegroundService.requestNotificationPermission();
  await CompanionForegroundService.start();
}

Future<void> disconnect() async {
  _holdLink = false;
  await client.disconnect();
}
```

```dart
// shell_controller.dart:106-112
Future<void> _loadStores() async {
  await RideRecordStore().load();
  await NavRouteStore().load();
  await FavoriteStore().load();
  await GpxLibraryStore().load();
  rideTick.value++;
}
```
`_loadStores` is called from `onInit` (line 80) and from `reloadLocal()` (146-148), which **has no callers anywhere** in `lib/`.

**UI shown while auto-reconnecting: essentially none.**
- The only widget that renders `conn` at all is `DevicePage` (`device_page.dart:118-153`). If the user is on the ride/settings tab, on a pushed page, or the shell was never built, the state change is invisible. There is no global indicator, no app bar badge, no toast.
- On failure: nothing. `_tryReconnect` swallows exceptions with `AppLog.w('Shell', '自动重连失败: $e')`; `CompanionClient._connectInternal` catches its own errors and sets `CompanionConnState.error` (`companion_client.dart:268-274`), and `DevicePage` maps `error` to the else-branch → `deviceDisconnected` ("未连接"). So the user sees either "正在连接…" transiently on the device tab, or a stale "未连接", and never a reason.
- `CompanionConnState.error` is never rendered as error text anywhere in `lib/ui/` (only `companion_debug_page.dart:701` labels it in dev text).
- `LocaleKeys.deviceMismatchShort` ("协议不符") exists (`locale_keys.dart:305`) but is unused in UI — presumably intended for a compact badge.

## 5. `lib/ble/companion_client.dart` scan/connect API surface

- `enum CompanionConnState { disconnected, connecting, discovering, ready, versionMismatch, error }` (16-34).
- `Stream<CompanionConnState> get stateStream` (142); `Stream<CompanionStatus> get statusStream` (145); `CompanionConnState get state` (148).
- `bool get isReady` (166); `bool get isLinking` = connecting || discovering (184-186); `bool get autoReconnect` (189); `BluetoothDevice? get device` (163); `int get mtu` (160); `CompanionStatus? get lastStatus` (151); `CompanionDevInfo? get lastDevInfo` (154); `int? get deviceProtoVersion` (157); `bool get canRelayNotification` (173); `bool get canTransferFiles` (180).
- Scan:
  ```dart
  // 195-208
  Future<void> startScan({Duration timeout = const Duration(seconds: 15)}) async {
    await FlutterBluePlus.startScan(
      withServices: [CompanionProto.service],
      timeout: timeout,
    );
  }
  Future<void> stopScan() => FlutterBluePlus.stopScan();
  Stream<List<ScanResult>> get scanResults => FlutterBluePlus.scanResults;
  ```
  Filtering is by **service UUID `FF10`**, not by name (doc comment at 191-194 says names can be changed, UUIDs cannot).
- `Future<void> connect(BluetoothDevice device, {bool autoReconnect = true})` (214-226) — tears down, arms watchdog, then `_connectInternal()`.
- `Future<void> kickReconnect({bool resetBackoff = false})` (229-236) — no-op unless `_autoReconnect && _device != null`, and returns early if `isReady || isLinking || _connectInFlight`.
- `Future<void> disconnect()` (1618-1622) sets `_autoReconnect = false`, tears down, sets `disconnected`.

**Name-based helpers do exist**, in `lib/ble/companion_proto.dart`:
- `static const advNamePrefix = 'Helm One-'` (52)
- `static const scanKeywords = ['Helm One', 'MyBike']` (55)
- `static bool matchesAdvName(String name)` (58-64) — case-insensitive contains of `helm one`, `helmone`, `mybike`, `vela`.

`BleManager` (`lib/ble/ble_manager.dart`) is the thin facade the scan page uses: `adapterState` (27), `isSupported()` (40), `requestPermissions()` (45-63, Android scan+connect+location / iOS bluetooth), `turnOn()` (66), `startScan({withKeywords = CompanionProto.scanKeywords, timeout})` (75-83), `stopScan()` (86), `scanResults` (89).

So a "scan and pick" UI today has both flavors available: service-UUID scan via `CompanionClient`, or keyword scan + `matchesAdvName` filter via `FlutterBluePlus`/`BleManager`. `ScanResult` gives `device.remoteId.str`, `device.platformName`, `device.advName`, `rssi`, `advertisementData.connectable`.

